{% set ux = doc.experience %}
<section id="overview" class="hero" aria-labelledby="overview-title">
  <div class="hero-top"><span class="eyebrow">Classic Era / {{ doc.zone }}</span><span class="snapshot-label">Saved {{ doc.scope }} snapshot · offline ready</span></div>
  <h1 id="overview-title" tabindex="-1"><span class="character-name">{{ doc.character }}</span> <span class="view-title">{{ page }}</span></h1>
  <p class="character-context"><strong>{{ doc.class_name }}{% if doc.selected_spec %} · {{ 'Tank' if doc.selected_spec == 'Guardian' else doc.selected_spec }}{% endif %}</strong><span class="faction-label">{{ ux.faction }}{% if ux.faction_level == 'inferred' %} · inferred{% elif ux.faction == 'Unknown' %} faction{% elif ux.faction_level == 'unknown' %} · evidence unknown{% endif %}</span><span>{{ doc.realm }}</span></p>
  <p class="hero-purpose">{{ 'Know what to change. Arrive with a plan.' if page == 'playbook' else 'Understand the fight. Follow the evidence.' }}</p>
  <div class="raid-pulse"><div><strong>{{ ux.attention_count }}<span> / {{ ux.bosses|length }}</span></strong><span>bosses with findings</span></div><div><strong>{{ ux.finding_count }}</strong><span>supported findings</span></div><div><strong>{{ ux.personal_count }}</strong><span>personal encounters</span></div></div>
  <div class="quality-strip"><strong>{{ ux.coverage }}</strong><span>{{ ux.limited_count }} boss{{ 'es' if ux.limited_count != 1 else '' }} with limited or unavailable comparisons</span><a href="#analysis-quality">See limits ↓</a></div>
</section>
<section class="priorities" aria-labelledby="priorities-title">
  <div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Start here</div><h2 id="priorities-title">{{ 'Your next raid priorities' if page == 'playbook' else 'What deserves your attention' }}</h2></div><span class="muted">Existing findings · highest severity first</span></div>
  <ol class="priority-list">
  {% for p in ux.priorities %}<li><span class="priority-number" aria-hidden="true">0{{ loop.index }}</span><div><div class="priority-meta"><span class="severity-label sev-{{ p.severity }}">{{ p.severity|capitalize }} severity</span><span>{{ p.confidence|capitalize }} confidence</span><span>{{ p.control }}</span>{% if p.get('benchmark', {}).get('n_known') is not none and p.benchmark.n_known < 4 %}<span class="unknown">Limited sample · {{ p.benchmark.n_known }} known</span>{% endif %}</div><h3><a href="#{{ p.boss_anchor }}">{{ p.heading }}</a></h3><p>{{ p.recommendation }}</p><details class="priority-why"><summary>Why this priority?</summary><p>{{ p.finding }}</p>{% if p.limitations %}<ul>{% for limit in p.limitations %}<li>{{ limit }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}</details><a class="priority-location" href="#{{ p.boss_anchor }}">{{ p.boss_name }}{% if p.boss_count > 1 %} · flagged on {{ p.boss_count }} bosses{% endif %} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></li>
  {% else %}<li><div><h3>No supported priority to rank</h3><p>Check personal data and comparison coverage below. No finding does not mean every aspect of your performance was assessed.</p></div></li>{% endfor %}
  </ol>
  {% if ux.priorities %}<p class="table-note">One example per finding type. Priorities retain the analysis severity; they do not predict a DPS or HPS gain. All findings remain under each boss.</p>{% endif %}
</section>
<section class="boss-triage" aria-labelledby="triage-title">
  <div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">Choose your encounter</div><h2 id="triage-title">Raid at a glance</h2></div><a href="{{ 'report' if page == 'playbook' else 'playbook' }}.html">{{ 'Investigate in Report' if page == 'playbook' else 'Prepare with Playbook' }} →</a></div>
  <div class="triage-list">{% for b in ux.bosses %}<a class="triage-row" href="#{{ b.anchor }}" data-boss-link="{{ b.anchor }}"><span class="triage-boss"><strong>{{ b.name }}</strong><span>{{ b.kill }} · {{ b.finding_count }} findings</span></span><span class="triage-state"><b>{{ b.state }}</b><span class="review-state" data-review-for="{{ b.anchor }}"></span></span><span class="triage-quality">{{ b.quality }}<small>{{ b.sources }} comparable sources{% if b.membership_label %} · {{ b.membership_label }}{% endif %}</small>{% if b.quality_note %}<small>{{ b.quality_note }}</small>{% endif %}</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>{% endfor %}</div>
</section>
<details id="analysis-quality" class="analysis-quality"><summary>How complete is this analysis?</summary><div><p>{{ ux.coverage_note }}</p><p>Comparison counts describe eligible entries. Each measurement has its own known sample; three known values are needed for a median. Three-value samples still carry a limited-sample label. Other-faction entries remain context.</p><dl class="kv">{% for label, value in doc.coverage %}<dt>{{ label }}</dt><dd>{{ value }}</dd>{% endfor %}</dl><ul>{% for limit in doc.limitations %}<li>{{ limit }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></div></details>
